Well, After 9 months or so I've managed my first ascension.

Tonya the Valk ascended to demigoddesshood last night roughly
65000 moves after beginning.  All my stats were pretty high
AC:-39 STR:25 DEX:18 CON:18 PWR:190(?) CHR:13  INT:13  WIS:17

(I know some of you pride yourself on the wimpiest ascension,
I just wanted to make it)

with roughly 500000 points.  I didn't bother keeping any gems 
or carrying gold.

I was made the EoB before entering Gehennom and wound up having
blessed rustproof +6 Vorpal Blade and Mjollnir.  In addition having
a blessed +4 ring of increase damage added an extra punch (I think).

Some Spoilers may follow





I think everything I did was 'legal'.  I didn't save/restore or
paralyze the WoY.  I did polypile and got a cloak of protection and
shield of reflection for my efforts.  

Life was made easier with 2 blessed magic lamps and two thrones which
game me wishes plus the wand in the castle for a total of nine.  

I managed to genocide Master Lich's early on.

I used up my only AoLS on the Fire Plane when stunned by an Archon I
wandered into a lava pit then surrounded by many E's D's A's and other
nasties.

Things I learned:
(1) I like Vorpal Blade. I thought I was doomed on the Atral plane
    when luckily it took the head off of Pestilence and Death.  

(2) AoMB is essential if only to forgive some mistakes.

(3) Rings of Lev are also very handy.  I didn't know that I would need
    it in the Air Plane.  I started to kick the monsters to move.  Then
    I thought Hmmm, maybe this will make it easier.

(4) The fire level was the hardest of all.  I couldn't find the portal.
    I had no scrolls of gold detection.  Then I realized I could wrest
    one last wish from my wand.

(5) The water level was easy but I just wandered around until I just
    happened to find the portal.  Just lucky I guess.

(6) Pickup all the food you can... and leave it in strategic places so
    you can get it on the way back up.

(7) Map out all the levels of the mazes (at least between the stairs) and
    dig yourself an easy path before going up to get the book from the wiz.
    Minimizing the moves gives him less time to pester you.  I saved all
    my wands of death to kill him (and his evil twin).  I killed him
    14 times.


There's alot more but I won't bore you any longer.  Thanks dev. team for
a great game.  I wonder what else you'll come up with in the next versions.

